A lightweight, browser-based reaction time test built with vanilla web technologies. Test your reflexes, track your recent scores, and try to beat your own average!
🎮 How to Play

    Open the game in any modern web browser.

    Press the W key to begin.

    The screen will turn red, indicating that you should wait.

    As soon as the screen turns green and says "Press W NOW!", hit the W key as fast as you can.

    If you press it too early, you'll get a "Too Soon!" warning and will need to restart the round.

    Complete 3 rounds to get your average reaction time.

✨ Features

    Simple Controls: Uses a single key press (W) for all interactions.

    Visual Cues: High-contrast background color changes (Red to Green) to signal the player.

    Anti-Cheat: Detects early key presses and resets the current round.

    Score Tracking: Calculates the average reaction time over 3 rounds

🛠️ Technologies Used

    HTML5: Page structure and layout.

    CSS3: Styling, transparency effects, and responsive layout.

    JavaScript (Vanilla): Game logic, state management, timing functions (setTimeout, Date.now()), and DOM manipulation.

🚀 Getting Started

    Clone or download this repository.

    Double-click the OneKeyReaction.html file to open it in your default web browser.

    Start pressing W!